# Shared Sentry Crons DSN for ST host systemd timers (installed as
# /etc/default/st-host-cron-sentry).  Mode 0600 on the host.  Populate from
# Infisical service tokens / the same fleet-infra project as scripts/sentry-ci-report.py.
#
# SENTRY_CRONS_DSN is preferred; SENTRY_FLEET_DSN is accepted as a fallback name.
# One of them is required: with neither set (and SENTRY_CRONS_DISABLED unset)
# the wrapper exits 78 without running the job, and the installers refuse to
# change any units.
# SENTRY_FLEET_DSN=
# SENTRY_CRONS_DSN=
#
# Set to 1 to run the jobs without check-ins.  This does NOT pause the
# schedule on the Sentry side: pause or delete the matching Sentry Crons
# monitors (st-host-litestream-l1-boundary-trim,
# st-host-st-container-restart-monitor) BEFORE setting it, or Sentry pages on
# every missed check-in.  The wrapper logs a warning on each disabled run.
# SENTRY_CRONS_DISABLED=0
